  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 103 PM EDT Thu Oct 29 2026\n\nFor the next few days, the pleasant fall weather will continue. A\nmid/upper level shortwave ridge will be crossing the region\nthrough Friday, with a low level ridge over the Appalachians. The\nmain concern each day will be early morning fog, primarily near \narea lakes and rivers. \n\nThe upper ridge shifts east and a shortwave trough approaches \nfrom the west on Sunday. Moisture and lift will be mainly in the\nmid and upper levels, while the sub-850 mb layer remains dry for\nthe eastern half of the area. Some light rain will likely reach \nthe ground in the Plateau and southern TN Valley, maybe a tenth to\na quarter inch, but NE sections will probably only see a trace to\na couple hundredths through Sunday night. Overcast mid/high clouds\non Sunday will hold high temperatures back in the 60s in most \nspots.\n\nDry and mild conditions return Monday and continue through at\nleast Tuesday, possibly Wednesday. Another stronger system may\nbring higher rain chances to the area late Wednesday and \nThursday. The ECMWF shows a deep, negatively tilted trough \ncrossing the Plains and MS Valley in this time frame. One thing to\nkeep an eye on with this system will be mountain wave winds, \nmainly Wednesday night.",
